  "title": "I cannot log in to VPN due to invalid password",
  "original_html": "<div class=\"entry-content\">\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<p>If you cannot connect to the VPN after following the <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/how-do-i-connect-to-pulse-secure-vpn-with-duo-2fa/\">How-Do-I-Connect-to-Pulse-Secure-VPN-with-Duo-2FA</a> instructions, you may need to reset your VPN profile settings. To clear the saved settings, follow the steps below:</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> Open the Pulse Secure client.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong>. Right click on the VPN profile and choose <strong>Forget Saved Settings</strong>.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1124\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"434\" sizes=\"(max-width: 322px) 100vw, 322px\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-56-38-AM.png\" srcset=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-56-38-AM.png 322w, https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-56-38-AM-297x400.png 297w\" width=\"322\"/></figure>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> In the pop-up window, click OK.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1125\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"177\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-58-53-AM.png\" width=\"344\"/></figure>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong>. Click Connect on the VPN Profile.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1126\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"434\" sizes=\"(max-width: 322px) 100vw, 322px\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-59-47-AM.png\" srcset=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-59-47-AM.png 322w, https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-59-47-AM-297x400.png 297w\" width=\"322\"/></figure>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<p><strong>Step 5.</strong> Enter your <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/how-do-i-connect-to-pulse-secure-vpn-with-duo-2fa/\">credentials</a> and click Connect. Do not click Save Settings.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1127\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"333\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 434px) 100vw, 434px\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-12-01-10-PM.png\" srcset=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-12-01-10-PM.png 434w, https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-12-01-10-PM-400x307.png 400w\" width=\"434\"/></figure>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\" style=\"height:10px\"></div>\n<p>Back to <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/duo-two-factor-authentication/#tab-strongfrequentlyaskedquestionsstrong\">FAQ page</a></p>\n<div class=\"entry-links\"></div>\n</div>",
  "html": "\n<p>If you cannot connect to the VPN after following the <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/how-do-i-connect-to-pulse-secure-vpn-with-duo-2fa/\">How-Do-I-Connect-to-Pulse-Secure-VPN-with-Duo-2FA</a> instructions, you may need to reset your VPN profile settings. To clear the saved settings, follow the steps below:</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> Open the Pulse Secure client.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong>. Right click on the VPN profile and choose <strong>Forget Saved Settings</strong>.</p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-56-38-AM.png\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> In the pop-up window, click OK.</p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-58-53-AM.png\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong>. Click Connect on the VPN Profile.</p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-11-59-47-AM.png\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 5.</strong> Enter your <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/how-do-i-connect-to-pulse-secure-vpn-with-duo-2fa/\">credentials</a> and click Connect. Do not click Save Settings.</p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2024/01/7-29-2021-12-01-10-PM.png\"/></figure>\n<p>Back to <a href=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/duo-two-factor-authentication/#tab-strongfrequentlyaskedquestionsstrong\">FAQ page</a></p>\n",
  "text": "If you cannot connect to the VPN after following the How-Do-I-Connect-to-Pulse-Secure-VPN-with-Duo-2FA instructions, you may need to reset your VPN profile settings. To clear the saved settings, follow the steps below: Step 1. Open the Pulse Secure client. Step 2 . Right click on the VPN profile and choose Forget Saved Settings . Step 3. In the pop-up window, click OK. Step 4 . Click Connect on the VPN Profile. Step 5. Enter your credentials and click Connect. Do not click Save Settings. Back to FAQ page",
